# The durable Vault's auto-unseal seal, for a deployed render of this module's
# own `vault` service.
#
# Vault agent 0.0.37 renders two shapes. Every deployed (restricted) profile
# gets the durable one: `vault server` with integrated raft storage on a
# PersistentVolumeClaim, auto-unsealed by the seal the environment supplies. The
# in-memory `vault server -dev` shape is the ephemeral local-apply render only.
#
# Read that guarantee precisely: it is the RENDERER that will not emit a dev
# command for a deployed profile. The image itself does not refuse one — run it
# directly with `server -dev` and deployed-context variables and it comes up on
# `storage_type: inmem` quite happily, because the exit-78 refusal below guards
# only the durable launch path. A `-dev` command that reached a deployed runtime
# by some route other than this render would therefore still start. Closing that
# belongs to the Vault launch owner (the `vault` service agent), not here.
#
# A durable Vault with no auto-unseal seal would come up sealed after every
# restart with nobody holding its unseal keys, so the agent refuses to start
# instead (`provision/server.sh`, exit 78, naming the variables below), and it
# refuses VAULT_SEAL_TYPE=shamir for the same reason. The keys must therefore be
# DECLARED here: an environment can supply a value for a key the module
# declares, but a key it never declares is inert.
#
# None of these is a secret — a seal names a KMS key, it does not hold one; the
# seal authenticates as the pod's workload identity. Values are supplied by the
# deployment environment, which is why every assignment here is empty.
#
# Set VAULT_SEAL_TYPE to the cloud's KMS seal and fill only that seal's own
# variables; the others stay empty and inert.
#
#   awskms   — AWS_REGION, VAULT_AWSKMS_SEAL_KEY_ID
#   gcpckms  — GOOGLE_PROJECT, GOOGLE_REGION,
#              VAULT_GCPCKMS_SEAL_KEY_RING, VAULT_GCPCKMS_SEAL_CRYPTO_KEY
#
# A consumer whose deployed environment is not named `aws` needs this same file
# under its own environment name; this directory is named for the `aws` target in
# this repository's own workspace.codefly.yaml.
#
# A cell that would rather bind a Vault it already runs does not need any of
# this: it declares `vault` as a managed service of kind `cell-vault` instead
# (module/deployment/README.md), and this module renders no Vault at all.
#
# Either way the listener is plaintext — in-cluster transport security is the
# mesh's, not a service's — so accounts reaches it over http under the
# composition's internal-transport/mesh-protected=true assertion, and there is
# no certificate, CA bundle or mounted file anywhere in that binding.
VAULT_SEAL_TYPE=

# awskms
AWS_REGION=
VAULT_AWSKMS_SEAL_KEY_ID=

# gcpckms
GOOGLE_PROJECT=
GOOGLE_REGION=
VAULT_GCPCKMS_SEAL_KEY_RING=
VAULT_GCPCKMS_SEAL_CRYPTO_KEY=

# Optional. A PGP *public* key the agent encrypts the recovery keys to when it
# initializes a durable server, so the init record is not readable from the
# volume. Recovery keys are the break-glass path when the seal's KMS key is
# lost; record their custody per the cell's runbook and never print them.
VAULT_RECOVERY_PGP_KEY=
